<figure class="spool-diagram">
	<svg
		viewBox="0 0 820 250"
		role="img"
		aria-label="An envelope starts in CAPTURED. It moves to PERSISTED on EnvelopePersisted, or to QUARANTINED on EnvelopeQuarantined or after three retries. While it waits in CAPTURED longer than the threshold it is published again. A PERSISTED envelope is deleted from the inbox after the TTL."
	>
		<defs>
			<marker id="es-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
				<path class="arrowhead" d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" />
			</marker>
		</defs>

		<rect class="box" x="40" y="104" width="150" height="44" rx="22" />
		<text class="name" x="115" y="131" text-anchor="middle">CAPTURED</text>

		<rect class="box" x="380" y="30" width="150" height="44" rx="22" />
		<text class="name" x="455" y="57" text-anchor="middle">PERSISTED</text>

		<rect class="box" x="380" y="178" width="150" height="44" rx="22" />
		<text class="name" x="455" y="205" text-anchor="middle">QUARANTINED</text>

		<rect class="external" x="650" y="30" width="150" height="44" rx="22" />
		<text class="name" x="725" y="57" text-anchor="middle">deleted</text>

		<path class="edge" d="M95,104 C95,52 135,52 135,101" marker-end="url(#es-arrow)" />
		<text class="small" x="150" y="62">published again after the threshold</text>

		<line class="edge" x1="190" y1="118" x2="377" y2="56" marker-end="url(#es-arrow)" />
		<text class="event-label" x="300" y="112" text-anchor="middle">EnvelopePersisted</text>

		<line class="edge" x1="190" y1="136" x2="377" y2="196" marker-end="url(#es-arrow)" />
		<text class="event-label" x="250" y="196" text-anchor="middle">EnvelopeQuarantined</text>
		<text class="small" x="250" y="212" text-anchor="middle">or three retries</text>

		<line class="edge" x1="530" y1="52" x2="647" y2="52" marker-end="url(#es-arrow)" />
		<text class="small" x="589" y="42" text-anchor="middle">after the TTL</text>
	</svg>
	<figcaption>
		The janitor moves an envelope between states when it sees the ingester's events. It also publishes again the envelopes that wait too long and deletes the ones already in the data lake once their TTL has passed.
	</figcaption>
</figure>
